# Send www and plain http straight to https://mediatraffics.com in one hop
http://www.mediatraffics.com/*   https://mediatraffics.com/:splat   301!
https://www.mediatraffics.com/*  https://mediatraffics.com/:splat   301!
http://mediatraffics.com/*       https://mediatraffics.com/:splat   301!

# Reputation pages: static HTML in public/<slug>/index.html. The no-slash URL is the
# canonical, so it is force-rewritten (200!). Without the ! Netlify 301s it to the
# slash URL first, and crawlers that don't follow redirects see an empty page.
/media-traffics-reviews    /media-traffics-reviews/index.html    200!
/media-traffics-reviews/   /media-traffics-reviews/index.html    200
/about-yousif-alias        /about-yousif-alias/index.html        200!
/about-yousif-alias/       /about-yousif-alias/index.html        200
/case-studies              /case-studies/index.html              200!
/case-studies/             /case-studies/index.html              200
/is-media-traffics-legit   /is-media-traffics-legit/index.html   200!
/is-media-traffics-legit/  /is-media-traffics-legit/index.html   200

# /, /privacy, /terms, /refund-policy and the guide pages are written to
# dist/<route>.html by scripts/prerender.mjs. Netlify serves /privacy from
# privacy.html on its own, so they need no rule here.

# Anything else is a real 404
/*    /404.html   404
